    "reasoning": "All 16 stated answers are mathematically correct and supported by their own captured worked solutions. One explanatory source error occurs in q-20869: after substitution, the solution says to set the lower bound to a and take a→−∞, but the transformed integral requires an upper bound a→∞. Its displayed calculation and final answer −1/2 are correct, so there is no answer disagreement. Mathematics: q-106896 gives Av=(2,k+1)=(2k,2k), hence k=1. q-158440 requires 4/k=1, hence k=4. q-109049 and q-109048 have variance zero because their arguments are constants. For q-129389, E[X²]=13/4 and Var[X]=3, giving scaled variance 1. q-129386 gives (10/3)²(3.6)=40. q-108940 gives 4²(8)=128. q-129399 gives E[X²]=1 and Var[X]=7/16, hence 16Var[X]=7. q-152758 has antiderivative −5/x and value 5/3. q-152754 has antiderivative −1/(2√t) and value √2/4. q-20869 has antiderivative −1/(2+x⁴) and value −1/2. For q-101736, integrals I and III both equal 1/2, whereas II diverges to positive infinity. q-6034 diverges because ln(a)−ln(6)→∞. q-76910 has speed 1+3t² and length 130. q-127573 has speed √2eᵗ and length √2(e^(π/2)−1). q-81678 gives v(t)=2t−t³+C; v(1)=4 implies C=3. No submitted grades or earlier answers were supplied; the MA evidence below comes exclusively from the captured worked solutions.",
